WEBVTT

00:00:00.950 --> 00:00:03.480
This is Mr. Sasano's ability...

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:05.860
The world within photographs...

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:09.360
It was torn from outside of the angle of view, huh?

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:07.190
This is no fun!

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:09.560
Don't you have anything to say?

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:13.020
You know, something like "Please give back Asai!",
while you're screaming and crying.

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:15.900
I don't need to worry about Kei.

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:18.200
I don't believe that Kei would ever lose to you.

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:20.450
Wake up and smell the coffee a bit more!

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:22.530
So, where's Asai?

00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:27.290
<i>That's more than enough. It's been five seconds.</i>

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:30.250
<i>We're friends.</i>

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:34.420
<i>We've been the bestest of friends for a long time.</i>

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:40.970
Hey there, Misora!

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:42.890
Good evening.

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:45.720
When did we first meet?

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:48.350
Well...

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:52.980
...earlier today.

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:55.360
<i>Her memory hasn't changed!</i>

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:57.650
We're friends, right?

00:02:57.650 --> 00:02:59.200
A memory like that exists,

00:02:59.200 --> 00:02:59.570
NO TRESSPASSING

00:02:59.570 --> 00:02:59.650
but it's fake.
NO TRESSPASSING

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:02.280
but it's fake.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:03.740
What makes you think that?

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:07.330
Kei says so.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:14.210
He predicted the pattern
in your memory manipulation

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:17.840
and pre-recorded his words to negate it.

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:20.800
I will keep listening to Kei's voice forever.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:25.430
Between my memory and Kei's words,
it's clear which one I should believe.

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:27.180
NO TRESSPASSING
What the hell? That's ridiculous!

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:28.430
But it's the truth.

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:33.900
In that case, I'll take all of your memories!

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:42.070
Full body. Ability.

00:03:42.070 --> 00:03:42.660
What?!

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:46.200
With that, I'm immune to all abilities.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:47.990
Your memory manipulation included.

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:50.290
Why are you here?!

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:52.540
Asai asked me to.

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:55.960
He expected Haruki to get attacked,
so he wanted me to stage a dramatic rescue.

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:58.210
But that's just weird!

00:03:58.210 --> 00:04:00.920
I've been watching my surroundings
from the top of this lighthouse!

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:02.220
I would have known if you came!

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:04.970
I had been sticking close behind you.

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:08.600
Before you reached the top of the lighthouse,
I was already hiding in here.

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:10.180
That's all. Any questions?

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:15.520
I'm good. I got it.

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:17.270
I'll take you down, too!

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:21.070
You used your ability again on Haruki earlier.

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:23.650
Since that erased the previous memory-altering effect,

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:25.780
Haruki regained her ability to reset.

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:28.370
He already accomplished his goal.

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:31.750
All that's left is for us to go straight home.

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:38.090
Everything went exactly as Asai planned,
from start to finish.

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:43.130
I'll say this again,
but Asai Kei is way stronger than you.

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:45.760
I don't like it.

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:46.970
What's that supposed to mean?

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:49.060
Exactly that.

00:04:49.060 --> 00:04:52.140
I don't like Asai being stronger than me.

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:54.190
I'll deny it. I can't accept it!

00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:56.940
That's the source of your downfall.

00:04:56.940 --> 00:05:01.440
I'm speaking from experience, so I already
know it's pointless to go up against Asai.

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:05.450
You were outclassed before
the battle had even begun.

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:08.620
NO TRESSPASSING
If we're not fighting yet, then I haven't lost.

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:11.830
It's fine if that's the way you wanna think.
NO TRESSPASSING

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:12.580
NO TRESSPASSING

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:14.330
I've had enough. I'm going home.
NO TRESSPASSING

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:14.790
NO TRESSPASSING

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:19.540
<i>I need power... something stronger!</i>

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:32.270
Everything's done and over with.

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:52.370
Should we reset?

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:58.210
If you say you're fine with the way things
are now, then I don't want to reset.

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:04.840
I want to remember losing my ability
and your promise to get it back for me.

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:07.300
Okay. Let's save.

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:08.840
Thank you very much.

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:11.720
Save.

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:17.350
Save. It's August 8th, 9:28:55 p.m.

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:29.030
<i>What are you doing?</i>

00:06:29.030 --> 00:06:30.910
I was looking at the cherry blossoms.

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:32.370
Cherry blossoms?

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:34.990
But you won't see them by looking at your feet.

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:37.000
That's true.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:39.080
I saw the tree first.

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:41.830
When I saw the cherry tree covered in flower petals,

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:43.840
I thought it was so beautiful.

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:46.050
And then, the wind swept them away.

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:50.510
The petals were fluttering in the wind,
and I found that even more beautiful.

00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:54.890
I was happy for some reason,
so I continued to watch them twirl in the sky.

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:58.730
As the petals landed on the ground,
I finally noticed something.

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:03.770
I wondered why they were still so beautiful,
despite stepping on them.

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:06.820
Were you sad about that?

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:08.360
I'm not really sure.

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:12.370
But I wanted to cry a little.

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:17.330
Say, do you think this is beautiful?

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:20.460
No, I don't.

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:21.830
Me neither.

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:25.960
I'm sure that's why I felt like crying.

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:28.550
It's okay to cry.

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:32.390
Yeah. Thank you.

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:35.640
Can you tell me a story?

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:37.220
What kind of story would you like?

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:41.640
I'd like a story about two people
who fulfill their promise to meet again.

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:42.900
Let's see...

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:46.820
There was once a witch in a faraway land.

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:49.820
Is she good or bad?

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:51.320
She's a good witch.

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:55.450
But everyone thought she was evil.

00:07:55.450 --> 00:07:58.910
The witch flies through the sky on a broom

00:07:58.910 --> 00:08:01.870
to see her beloved who
she promised to reunite with.

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:08.630
It's been 50 years since then, huh?

00:08:08.630 --> 00:08:12.630
Second Time
Wednesday
August 9th

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:16.510
<i>In the previous timeline,
there were two things that happened today.</i>

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:20.930
<i>The first was that Mr. Sasano said
he wanted me to give him the MacGuffin,</i>

00:08:20.930 --> 00:08:23.940
<i>so I accepted his request to restore the ability he lost.</i>

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:26.900
<i>And the other thing was being
summoned by the Witch.</i>

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:29.400
<i>Those two are hiding something.</i>

00:08:29.610 --> 00:08:32.490
<i>At the very least, Mr. Sasano is lying.</i>

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:37.620
<i>It's possible to enter his photos
without the use of any ability.</i>

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:40.040
<i>He doesn't need the MacGuffin.</i>

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:51.300
"Come see me right away.
The other two are presents."

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:15.820
This is it.

00:09:27.630 --> 00:09:31.050
Are you... Asai Kei?

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:34.420
Yes. I came here through Mr. Sasano's ability.

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:36.470
Why?

00:09:36.470 --> 00:09:39.760
I was under the impression that you summoned me.

00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:44.480
This is a future I didn't see.

00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:47.810
That means I betrayed myself, huh?

00:09:47.810 --> 00:09:49.610
What do you mean?

00:09:49.610 --> 00:09:55.110
I believe the me in some other photo
made arrangements for you to come here.

00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:59.030
I'm sure it was to make my plan fail.

00:09:59.030 --> 00:10:00.830
Your plan?

00:10:01.030 --> 00:10:04.700
Yes. I'm currently working toward one plan.

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:09.170
I will be confined by the Bureau
for the next 28 years.

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:13.590
And those years represent
how much time I have left.

00:10:14.420 --> 00:10:19.390
I accepted that I would die while
being confined by the Bureau.

00:10:19.390 --> 00:10:20.470
But...

00:10:20.470 --> 00:10:27.730
I decided to escape from the Bureau and reunite
with my beloved just for the final week of my life.

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:32.520
However, the Bureau won't allow
me to be free for even a week.

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:33.520
That's why...

00:10:34.940 --> 00:10:39.530
Sorry. I decided to use you both.

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:41.320
Me and who?

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:44.540
A girl named Oka Eri.

00:10:45.830 --> 00:10:49.790
She wanted an ability far greater
than the ones you two possess.

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:54.500
She has her eyes dead set
on the ability to know the future,

00:10:54.800 --> 00:11:01.180
which is why I decided to escape
that building with Oka Eri's help.

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:03.470
Is that even possible?

00:11:03.470 --> 00:11:07.100
When I'm closer to death,
my security will become lax.

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:11.020
That means, with Oka Eri's memory manipulation,
your security will fall apart.

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:15.520
But if I wait for her to come, I won't make it in time.

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:19.700
By then, I'll already be on the verge
of death and be unable to walk.

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:23.070
That's why I needed to speed things up.

00:11:23.070 --> 00:11:27.830
By losing to you,
she'll be determined to take me away.

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:34.540
On August 9th at 9:18 p.m,
Oka Eri will appear before me.

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:39.420
And by telling me about that,
you're betraying yourself.

00:11:39.880 --> 00:11:43.390
When I'm abducted, she'll confront the Bureau.

00:11:43.890 --> 00:11:47.680
In Sakurada, there is only tragedy
for those who oppose the Bureau.

00:11:48.970 --> 00:11:51.810
Thank you for telling me.

00:11:52.100 --> 00:11:54.190
I told you because it has nothing to do with me.

00:11:54.190 --> 00:11:59.530
After all, the one who will
reunite with him is not me.

00:11:59.530 --> 00:12:01.030
I'm not the real one.

00:12:01.530 --> 00:12:05.070
I couldn't stand the guilt of doing
it for the other me, that's all.

00:12:05.530 --> 00:12:06.870
Farewell.

00:12:09.950 --> 00:12:13.500
<i>If things continue this way,
the Witch will be able to escape,</i>

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:16.040
<i>but Oka Eri will become an enemy of the Bureau.</i>

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:21.800
<i>If I stop Oka Eri, the Witch will remain
confined and pass away in a week.</i>

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:25.430
<i>I need to find a way to save the Witch
without anyone turning against the Bureau</i>

00:12:25.430 --> 00:12:28.260
<i>and let her reunite with Mr. Sasano.</i>

00:12:35.060 --> 00:12:36.400
This is Sasano.

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:39.570
Nice to meet you. I am Asai Kei.

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:42.280
You've heard about me from the Witch, right?

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:45.530
Sorry. I did something bad to you.

00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:46.280
Sorry.

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:49.410
Thank you for sending me the photos.

00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:51.040
What's your situation?

00:12:51.040 --> 00:12:56.380
The red-eyed girl came by again
and manipulated my memories.

00:12:56.380 --> 00:13:00.130
She made me send her all the pictures
I took with my ability.

00:13:00.130 --> 00:13:02.050
But I didn't have any photos left at home.

00:13:02.050 --> 00:13:03.760
I see.

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:09.010
But that means you remembered how
to use your ability in exchange, right?

00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:10.970
Yes, most likely.

00:13:10.970 --> 00:13:13.640
What are you going to do now, Mr. Sasano?

00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:17.350
I'll try asking the Bureau to let me see her.

00:13:17.350 --> 00:13:19.020
I can't think of anything else.

00:13:19.230 --> 00:13:22.900
I see. Please let me help you out, then.

00:13:28.870 --> 00:13:31.290
I heard from the Witch within the picture.

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:36.830
Oka Eri successfully infiltrates the building and
will come in contact with the Witch at 9:18 p.m.

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:41.210
So basically, if we follow right behind her,
we'll be able to go in, too.

00:13:41.210 --> 00:13:43.010
It's 9:10 p.m.

00:13:43.010 --> 00:13:43.670
She's here.

00:13:45.550 --> 00:13:46.470
Let's go.

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:50.930
Please take a picture of this corridor.

00:13:55.350 --> 00:13:58.650
We won't have guns pointed at us
the instant the door opens, will we?

00:13:58.650 --> 00:14:01.190
I really don't think they would have guns.

00:14:01.190 --> 00:14:06.200
If the Bureau seriously prepared security guards,
we wouldn't be able to come this far.

00:14:10.450 --> 00:14:12.330
It's 9:18 p.m.

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:14.910
Is this okay?

00:14:14.910 --> 00:14:17.500
No. A Bureau staff member is photographed.

00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:19.420
He'll be a nuisance within the photo.

00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:25.130
<i>One, two, three...</i>

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:27.050
Hold it right there, Oka Eri.

00:14:27.670 --> 00:14:28.680
Asai?!

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:30.760
Oka Eri, I've come to stop you.

00:14:31.010 --> 00:14:34.010
That's unnecessary. We'll handle everything here.

00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:35.970
Hurry up, hurry up!

00:14:35.970 --> 00:14:39.650
That's not going to work. Please let us talk to her.

00:14:39.940 --> 00:14:40.770
Stop right there.

00:14:42.230 --> 00:14:43.650
Full body. Ability.

00:14:49.070 --> 00:14:52.570
Do you understand what it means
to use an ability against us?

00:14:52.570 --> 00:14:56.540
Of course. But we couldn't think of another way.

00:14:56.790 --> 00:14:59.210
The Bureau won't forgive you.

00:14:59.210 --> 00:15:01.960
Would you be able to forget
everything for us, if possible?

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:03.920
That's impossible.

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:04.960
I see.

00:15:07.260 --> 00:15:08.510
Upper body. Gravity.

00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:09.510
Reset.

00:15:09.720 --> 00:15:10.340
Reset.

00:15:15.640 --> 00:15:19.690
It's August 8th, 9:28:55 p.m.

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:22.230
Looks like we've reset.

00:15:22.230 --> 00:15:23.810
Murase disappeared.

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:28.320
Let's go meet up with her. I know where she is.

00:15:33.070 --> 00:15:35.200
What are you thinking?

00:15:36.080 --> 00:15:40.660
So this means these photos
didn't get reset, just like me.

00:15:40.660 --> 00:15:44.670
Third Time
Wednesday
August 9th

00:16:04.060 --> 00:16:06.690
You will escape from here in a different way.

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:09.650
Please call me as quickly as possible.

00:16:09.650 --> 00:16:11.860
I'll bring these photos with me.

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:30.170
We reset.

00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:33.970
The things you planned for tonight will fail.

00:16:33.970 --> 00:16:40.220
I knew you'd reset, and I knew
you'd come to my rescue for sure.

00:16:41.270 --> 00:16:43.020
But that's no good.

00:16:43.520 --> 00:16:44.480
Why?

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:49.020
You're too weak. Eventually,
even I will become your weakness.

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:51.240
You can't be weak.

00:16:52.990 --> 00:16:55.030
When did you come back from a reset?

00:16:55.030 --> 00:16:56.530
Yesterday night.

00:16:56.530 --> 00:16:58.700
It still hasn't been 24 hours!

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:02.700
You're not supposed to see me at this time.

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:05.540
Save properly and take various precautions.

00:17:05.870 --> 00:17:09.540
You have to appear composed
enough to piss me off.

00:17:10.340 --> 00:17:15.010
It's true that I'm currently defenseless,
but there's no danger.

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:17.300
You won't do anything to me when I'm defenseless.

00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:19.390
You're so unfair.

00:17:19.390 --> 00:17:24.940
No matter how hard I try to fight
and beat you, you won't fight back.

00:17:25.140 --> 00:17:26.730
That's just how it is.

00:17:28.270 --> 00:17:31.150
You know, I tried really hard for two years.

00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:36.200
I changed the way I talked, changed my wardrobe,
and even bought colored contacts.

00:17:36.530 --> 00:17:41.120
I thought I'd see everything around me
in a different color if I wore them.

00:17:42.040 --> 00:17:43.450
Did your view change?

00:17:43.450 --> 00:17:44.870
Not in the slightest.

00:17:44.870 --> 00:17:48.960
There's no color on the colored
contacts where your pupils are.

00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:50.500
But I like them.

00:17:51.710 --> 00:17:54.970
When I look at the mirror,
I feel like the reflection isn't me.

00:17:55.340 --> 00:17:58.510
I see. I'm glad that you like it.

00:18:03.970 --> 00:18:07.100
There's someone who wants to see you.

00:18:07.100 --> 00:18:10.900
I believe a Bureau staff member
will be picking you up today at 4 p.m.

00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:12.070
Understood.

00:18:13.190 --> 00:18:17.030
Sooner or later, I'm going to find
an extravagant way to beat you.

00:18:17.530 --> 00:18:19.450
Okay. I'll be waiting.

00:18:20.070 --> 00:18:21.450
Don't!

00:18:22.030 --> 00:18:23.330
Be afraid instead.

00:18:29.290 --> 00:18:31.290
I'm from the Bureau.

00:18:31.290 --> 00:18:32.710
I've come to pick you up.

00:18:41.850 --> 00:18:43.350
It's been a long time.

00:18:43.890 --> 00:18:46.640
Or should I say, nice to meet you?

00:18:47.140 --> 00:18:49.810
May I ask what your name is?

00:18:49.810 --> 00:18:53.900
I'm sorry. I don't have one.

00:18:53.900 --> 00:18:56.530
I'm not sure how I should address you, then.

00:18:56.780 --> 00:19:01.160
I'm an entity that essentially needs no name.

00:19:01.700 --> 00:19:04.200
Call me "Witch," if you must.

00:19:04.200 --> 00:19:05.200
Yes, ma'am.

00:19:05.200 --> 00:19:06.830
Come a bit closer.

00:19:09.620 --> 00:19:10.870
Bend down a little.

00:19:15.750 --> 00:19:18.550
I wanted to see you, Asai Kei.

00:19:18.550 --> 00:19:20.930
I had always wanted to apologize to you.

00:19:22.260 --> 00:19:25.180
Would you be able to fall in love with a stone?

00:19:25.180 --> 00:19:27.220
No, I probably can't.

00:19:27.220 --> 00:19:30.230
Try thinking about the person you love, then.

00:19:30.230 --> 00:19:37.110
Let's imagine that girl as a pebble—
one that neither speaks nor moves.

00:19:37.110 --> 00:19:40.240
Imagine that she's a cold pebble that can only think.

00:19:40.820 --> 00:19:44.120
Could you fall in love with it?

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:46.330
My first answer was wrong.

00:19:46.790 --> 00:19:49.830
I'm sure I can fall in love even with a stone.

00:19:49.830 --> 00:19:53.250
What would you love about the stone?

00:19:53.250 --> 00:19:57.340
Well, our past and our lifetime of memories.

00:19:58.880 --> 00:20:01.220
I think the same goes for me, too.

00:20:01.760 --> 00:20:07.010
What I love might be an ordinary stone.

00:20:07.510 --> 00:20:09.850
Is that a sad thing?

00:20:09.850 --> 00:20:12.480
Yes, very sad.

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:17.400
I don't know if I actually love a person.

00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:23.530
Maybe I just want to believe
that I still love that someone.

00:20:23.530 --> 00:20:29.490
All I have is the past,
so I might just be in love with that past.

00:20:29.870 --> 00:20:34.080
Your beloved can't be an ordinary stone.

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:40.710
If I still do love a person,
I want to make sure of it, if possible.

00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:45.720
Looks like time's up.

00:20:45.720 --> 00:20:48.220
Is there anything you'd
like to ask me before you go?

00:20:50.520 --> 00:20:52.350
<i>Why are you a witch?</i>

00:20:53.850 --> 00:20:56.100
<i>It was something I heard a long time ago.</i>

00:20:56.440 --> 00:20:58.770
<i>A story of a witch who rode on a broom,</i>

00:20:58.770 --> 00:21:03.070
<i>flying through the sky to knock
on the window of her beloved's room.</i>

00:21:04.490 --> 00:21:08.160
<i>I've been longing to do that.</i>

00:21:30.430 --> 00:21:32.770
What are you going to do now?

00:21:33.100 --> 00:21:36.730
I'll leave Sakurada, forget about my ability,
and live out the rest of my life.

00:21:36.730 --> 00:21:38.610
It'll just be a week, though.

00:21:39.400 --> 00:21:42.190
Do you want to know your own future?

00:21:42.690 --> 00:21:43.490
Yes.

00:21:44.610 --> 00:21:47.610
Even if it's something painful?

00:21:48.030 --> 00:21:49.200
Yes, please.

00:21:50.370 --> 00:21:55.000
The witch, riding a broom,
knocks on the window of her beloved's room.

00:21:55.000 --> 00:21:56.790
What happens next?

00:21:57.120 --> 00:21:59.830
He hastily opens the window.

00:21:59.830 --> 00:22:01.000
And then...

00:22:03.760 --> 00:22:06.550
the two of them find happiness.

00:22:30.740 --> 00:22:34.240
You're going to be involved in something big...

00:22:34.740 --> 00:22:37.620
Something involving my successor.

00:22:37.620 --> 00:22:40.380
Does such a person exist?

00:22:40.630 --> 00:22:43.090
The Bureau has been looking
for one for a long time now.

00:22:43.090 --> 00:22:48.130
But no matter how much they looked,
they couldn't find anyone with the ability to see the future.

00:22:49.380 --> 00:22:50.260
However,

00:22:50.760 --> 00:22:53.810
you know someone who does possess it.

00:22:53.810 --> 00:22:56.560
You've met that person a little over two years ago.

00:22:57.140 --> 00:22:59.230
Is your successor...

00:22:59.230 --> 00:23:02.190
Is the future-seeing ability user a girl?

00:23:02.190 --> 00:23:03.150
Yes.

00:23:04.070 --> 00:23:08.780
A slender girl with short hair, big eyes,
and about the age of a middle schooler.

00:23:09.280 --> 00:23:10.030
Yes.

00:23:13.660 --> 00:23:17.290
Is it the girl who died two years ago?

00:23:17.500 --> 00:23:22.670
Correct. And you will run into her again.

00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:26.420
